","choreographer","record producer","actor"],"debut":"2001","agencies":[{"name":"YG Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q50595","start":"","end":""},{"name":"P Nation","korean":true,"id":"Q61410007","start":"","end":""},{"name":"Avex Group","korean":false,"id":"Q790686","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/42psy42/","x":"https://x.com/psy_oppa","youtube":"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCrDkAvwZum-UTjHmzDI2iIw","tiktok":"https://www.tiktok.com/@42psy42","spotify":"https://open.spotify.com/artist/2dd5mrQZvg6SmahdgVKDzh","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/f99b7d67-4e63-4678-aa66-4c6ac0f7d24a"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Park Jae-sang, better known as Psy ( SY; 싸이), is a South Korean singer, songwriter, and record producer. He has received numerous accolades, including an American Music Award, a World Music Award, and 10 MAMA Awards. He is the founder of the talent agency P Nation. Psy released his debut studio album Psy from the Psycho World! in 2001. He gained international prominence in 2012 with the hit single \"Gangnam Style\", which reached the top 10 on the U.S. Billboard Hot 100 and became a global viral phenomenon. Its music video was the first on YouTube to reach 1 billion views; it held the record for most-viewed YouTube video from November 2012 to July 2017.","title":"Psy","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Psy"}},"Q20779702":{"id":"Q20779702","name":"Jo Ka-eun","ko":"가은","birthName":"조가은","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Cho Ka-eun","Kaeun"],"birth":"1992-07-28","death":"","birthplace":"Masan","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","rapper","model"],"debut":"","agencies":[],"groups":[{"id":"Q492146","name":"Dal Shabet","start":"2011","end":"2015"}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/jjojjo_eun/","x":"https://x.com/shabet_kaeun","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/b19f9c33-6bc2-4532-b922-3ed8f056166b"},"photo":null,"bio":null},"Q21060406":{"id":"Q21060406","name":"Kim Chae-won","ko":"김채원","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Chae Won","Kim Chaewon"],"birth":"1997-11-08","death":"","birthplace":"Gongju","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","pop singer"],"debut":"2015","agencies":[{"name":"DSP Media","korean":true,"id":"Q489428","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q20858387","name":"April","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/chaeni_0824/","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/27570ac1-0dbf-49e0-befa-3fddad90ce94"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"April was a South Korean girl group formed by DSP Media. The group debuted on August 24, 2015, with their EP Dreaming and its title track \"Dream Candy\". The group's final lineup was composed of six members: Chaekyung, Chaewon, Naeun, Yena, Rachel, and Jinsol. The group officially disbanded on January 28, 2022.","title":"Kim Chae-won (singer, born 1997)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kim_Chae-won_%28singer%2C_born_1997%29"},"positions":["Main vocalist"],"factSources":{"positions":{"name":"Namu Wiki (2021 dump)","license":"CC BY-NC-SA 2.0 KR","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/2.0/kr/","base":"https://namu.wiki/w/","url":"https://namu.wiki/w/%EA%B9%80%EC%B1%84%EC%9B%90%28APRIL%29"}}},"Q236086":{"id":"Q236086","name":"Justin Chon","ko":"저스틴 전","birthName":"Justin Jitae Chon","birthNameEn":"Justin Jitae Chon","aliases":[],"birth":"1981-05-29","death":"","birthplace":"Garden Grove","nationality":["United States"],"height":170,"occupations":["film actor","television actor","singer","YouTuber","film director","screenwriter"],"debut":"2005","agencies":[],"groups":[{"id":"Q24909324","name":"Boys Generally Asian","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/justinchon/","x":"https://x.com/justinchon","youtube":"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCIXtoLknxvVZiZDnlQssfzg","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/be6993c6-95b9-4445-a469-0c177bd0c6c5"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Justin Jitae Chon is an American actor and filmmaker. He has directed four films, Gook (2017), Ms. Purple (2019), Blue Bayou (2021), and Jamojaya. He is also known for portraying Eric Yorkie in The Twilight Saga film series. He is a member of the K-pop parody group Boys Generally Asian.","title":"Justin Chon","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Chon"}},"Q27952182":{"id":"Q27952182","name":"Park Jang-hyun","ko":"박장현","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Park Jang-hyeon"],"birth":"1989-06-06","death":"","birthplace":"Cheonan","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"","agencies":[],"groups":[{"id":"Q25143919","name":"Vromance","start":"","end":""}],"links":{},"photo":null,"bio":null,"positions":["Leader","Vocalist"],"factSources":{"positions":{"name":"Namu Wiki (2021 dump)","license":"CC BY-NC-SA 2.0 KR","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/2.0/kr/","base":"https://namu.wiki/w/","url":"https://namu.wiki/w/%EB%B0%95%EC%9E%A5%ED%98%84"}}},"Q41967606":{"id":"Q41967606","name":"Jinho","ko":"진호","birthName":"Jo Jin-ho","birthNameEn":"Jo Jin-ho","aliases":["Cho Jin Ho","Jin Ho","Jino","Cho Jin-ho"],"birth":"1992-04-17","death":"","birthplace":"Bucheon","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"2016","agencies":[{"name":"Cube Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q484449","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q23936742","name":"Pentagon","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/jinho__jo/","x":"https://x.com/CUBE_PTG","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/ba162b5f-4296-4db1-bd2b-edd04470e34c"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Jo Jin-ho, commonly known by the mononym Jinho, is a South Korean singer, songwriter, composer, vocal coach and member of South Korean boy group Pentagon under Cube Entertainment. In 2023, he participated in the JTBC singing competition program Phantom Singer 4, where his quartet Crezl ultimately placed third and officially debuted. He is a former SM Entertainment trainee and member of the project group SM the Ballad. After leaving SM Entertainment in 2015, Jinho became a vocal coach. Since then, he has trained Cube labelmates (G)I-dle and Yoo Seon-ho, among others.","title":"Jinho","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jinho"},"positions":["Main vocalist"],"mbti":"ISTP","factSources":{"positions":{"name":"Namu Wiki (2021 dump)","license":"CC BY-NC-SA 2.0 KR","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/2.0/kr/","base":"https://namu.wiki/w/","url":"https://namu.wiki/w/%EC%A7%84%ED%98%B8%28%ED%8E%9C%ED%83%80%EA%B3%A4%29"},"mbti":{"name":"Namu Wiki (2021 dump)","license":"CC BY-NC-SA 2.0 KR","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/2.0/kr/","base":"https://namu.wiki/w/","url":"https://namu.wiki/w/%EC%A7%84%ED%98%B8%28%ED%8E%9C%ED%83%80%EA%B3%A4%29"}}},"Q429046":{"id":"Q429046","name":"Jay Park","ko":"박재범","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Park Jae Beom (박재범)"],"birth":"1987-04-25","death":"","birthplace":"Seattle","nationality":["United States","South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["songwriter","singer","actor","dancer","choreographer","model"],"debut":"2008","agencies":[{"name":"H1ghr Music","korean":true,"id":"Q55506796","start":"","end":""},{"name":"AOMG","korean":true,"id":"Q16164774","start":"","end":""},{"name":"JYP Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q483238","start":"","end":""},{"name":"Sony Music","korean":false,"id":"Q56760250","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q222760","name":"2PM","start":"2008","end":"2009"}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/jparkitrighthere/","x":"https://x.com/jaybumaom","youtube":"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCK5fO9Q2gitao0M5yQvPnvw","tiktok":"https://www.tiktok.com/@jayparkisoverparty","spotify":"https://open.spotify.com/artist/4XDi67ZENZcbfKnvMnTYsI","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/3dda8202-ce15-4031-862a-77bc6759d15e"},"photo